          "id": "f1bd99ed43a134383bc0be1d766a6f121601a499",
          "message": "[CBRD-27485] Fix partitioned SEMI/ANTI inner scans in parallel workers (#8011)\n\nhttp://jira.cubrid.org/browse/CBRD-27485\n\nPurpose\nFix incorrect EXISTS and NOT EXISTS results when parallel-scan workers probe a partitioned SEMI/ANTI join inner, and prevent failures when tracing is enabled.\n\nImplementation\npx_scan_task.cpp\nPrune partitioned SEMI/ANTI inner scans in each worker clone regardless of tracing.\nRewind the inner scan for each outer row with qexec_reset_sa_inner_scan_block.\nRestore a NULL curr_spec to spec_list before closing the scan in finalize.\n\nquery_executor.c, query_executor.h\nExpose qexec_reset_sa_inner_scan_block for use by parallel-scan workers.\n\nRemarks\nAdd HASH and RANGE partition regression coverage for EXISTS and NOT EXISTS, including trace-enabled execution, in CUBRID/cubrid-testcases#3574.",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-29T10:34:12Z",
          "tree_id": "f642f710ca24c8ccc5f43cf9cb867e46aa92bf28"
        },
